<% content_for :title, "Privacy" %>

<article class="max-w-2xl">
  <header class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">What Purple stores about you, why, and how to have it removed.</p>
  </header>

  <%= render "pages/draft_notice" %>

  <div class="space-y-8 leading-relaxed">
    <section aria-labelledby="who">
      <h2 id="who" class="text-xl font-bold">Who runs Purple</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Purple is run by <strong>[to confirm: name or company]</strong>, who is responsible for your
        data under UK data protection law. Questions and requests go to
        <strong>[to confirm: contact email]</strong>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="what">
      <h2 id="what" class="text-xl font-bold">What we store</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-ink-muted">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Your account:</strong> your email address, your display name and
          your password, which is stored only as a one-way hash that nobody can read back.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Sign-ins:</strong> for each device you're signed in on, its IP
          address and browser, so you can see and sign out your sessions on your account page.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Your play:</strong> the moves you make in shifts and Workshop
          campaigns, your scores, XP, levels, streaks and badges.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
        Everything inside the game is fictional. The staff numbers, passwords and other "private
        details" you can share in a shift are made up for your character, and the sign-in pages in
        the game never record what you type. Never enter a real password into a game page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="why">
      <h2 id="why" class="text-xl font-bold">Why</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        To run your account and the game: signing you in, scoring your play, keeping your progress and
        showing leaderboards. We email you only to confirm your address and to reset your password.
        There's no advertising, no tracking or analytics, and we don't sell or share your data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="public">
      <h2 id="public" class="text-xl font-bold">What other players see</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Your display name, levels, badges and preferred side are on your public profile, and on the
        leaderboards unless you opt out on your account page. Your email address is never shown.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="cookies">
      <h2 id="cookies" class="text-xl font-bold">Cookies</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        One cookie, to keep you signed in. It's needed for the site to work, so there's no cookie banner.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="where">
      <h2 id="where" class="text-xl font-bold">Where it's kept, and for how long</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        On a server hosted by <strong>[to confirm: hosting provider and country]</strong>. Emails are
        sent through <strong>[to confirm: email provider]</strong>. Database backups are
        kept in <strong>[to confirm: storage provider]</strong> for 30 days. Your data is kept while
        you have an account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rights">
      <h2 id="rights" class="text-xl font-bold">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete your account
        and everything linked to it, by emailing <strong>[to confirm: contact email]</strong>. If
        you're unhappy with how we handle your data, you can complain to the Information
        Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated <strong>[to confirm: date]</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</article>
